From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:30:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: allow QSEECom on the Pixel 2 XL

taimen's QSEE answers the QSEECom interface: the version query, which runs
before the machine allowlist, logged

    qseecom: found qseecom with version 0x1001000

on 2026-08-19. Allowlist the machine so the auxiliary device is created and
qcom_scm_qseecom_app_get_id() becomes reachable.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index ff73c51be6bf..fca851215737 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2362,6 +2362,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "dell,latitude-7455" },
 	{ .compatible = "dell,xps13-9345" },
 	{ .compatible = "ecs,liva-qc710" },
+	{ .compatible = "google,taimen" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-ultra-g1q" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-x14" },
 	{ .compatible = "huawei,gaokun3" },
